 {msg}←kind Unsupported(id class names);what;on;at;pfx;plural;cls;noun;quoted;stack;report
⍝ Report a ⎕WC feature EWC does not implement. kind is 'class', 'property' or 'name'.
⍝
⍝ EWC.UNSUPPORTED escalates: 0 session, 1 adds UNSUPPORTEDLOG, 2 adds a DOMAIN
⍝ ERROR. At 2 the result is the message and the CALLER must ⎕SIGNAL it - signalling
⍝ here would be caught by the cover's ⎕TRAP←0 'S' and suspend inside EWC.

 msg←''
 →(0=≢names←,⊆names)⍴0
 ⍝ ∆WS can hand us a non-character name when its argument parses as neither
 ⍝ shape. Coerce, or report becomes a mixed array and ⎕NPUT below fails.
 (id class names)←(⍕id)(⍕class)(⍕¨names)

 plural←1<≢names
 cls←class,(0≠≢class)/' '
 noun←(1+plural)⊃'property' 'properties'
 quoted←2↓∊', '∘,¨'"'∘,¨names,¨⊂'"' ⍝ 2↓ drops the leading separator

 :Select kind
 :Case 'class'
     what←'class ',quoted
 :Case 'property'
     what←cls,noun,' ',2↓∊', '∘,¨names
 :Case 'name'
     what←quoted,' ',((1+plural)⊃'is not a' 'are not'),' ',cls,noun
 :EndSelect

 on←(0≠≢id)/' on "',id,'"'
 stack←{(1<⍵⍳¨'[')/⍵}showCallStack ⍝ Drop unnamed frames, which format as just "[0]"
 at←(0≠≢stack)/' at ',1↓∊' '∘,¨(2⌊≢stack)↑stack
 report←'Unsupported on eWC: ',what,on,at,'. Please write to support@dyalog.com if you want this soon.'

 ⍝ Not 'U' Log: these are gated by UNSUPPORTED, not LOGMODES. Timestamp format
 ⍝ deliberately matches Log so the two read alike in a session.
 pfx←(,'ZI2,<:>,ZI2,<.>,ZI3' ⎕FMT 1 3⍴¯3↑⎕TS),' U:'
 :If 0≠≢LOGFILE ⍝ Documented to redirect all log output, so honour it here too
     (⊂pfx,' ',report)⎕NPUT LOGFILE 2
 :Else
     ⎕←pfx report
 :EndIf

 :If UNSUPPORTED≥1
 :AndIf 0≠≢UNSUPPORTEDLOG
     :Trap 0 ⍝ An unwritable log must not break the application
         :If 0=UNSUPPORTEDSEEN ⍝ The file is appended to forever - mark each run
             UNSUPPORTEDSEEN←1
             (⊂'')⎕NPUT UNSUPPORTEDLOG 2
             (⊂'=== EWC ',Version.Server,'  ',((1+MODE)⊃'desktop' 'browser' 'multi'),'  ',(⍕CODELOCATION),'  ',(,'ZI4,<->,ZI2,<->,ZI2,< >,ZI2,<:>,ZI2,<:>,ZI2'⎕FMT 1 6⍴6↑⎕TS))⎕NPUT UNSUPPORTEDLOG 2
         :EndIf
         (⊂pfx,' ',report)⎕NPUT UNSUPPORTEDLOG 2 ⍝ Catenated, not ⍕: this file gets emailed
     :Else
         'E'Log'Unable to write ',UNSUPPORTEDLOG
     :EndTrap
 :EndIf

 :If 2=UNSUPPORTED
     msg←report ⍝ The caller ⎕SIGNALs it; see the header
 :EndIf
